  "question": {
    "text": "Cathode rays of velocity <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> describe an approximate circular path of the radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> in an electric field <math><mn>300</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> If the velocity of cathode rays are doubled. The value of electric field so that the rays describe the same circular path, will be"
  },
